# ---- daily state hygiene (optional — every box) ----
# bin/disk-clean.sh (every cron/*.cron, 04:47Z) bounds the four things a box
# accumulates and nothing else removes (BH-1044). A value that is not a number
# logs one line and falls back to the default below; it is never clamped in
# silence. docs/verification-map/disk-clean-hygiene.md
# How much of state/closeout-aged-out.tsv is kept, in days of the 12-digit launch
# stamp in each row's build dir. An older row whose build dir is GONE (and a
# duplicate row for a dir already kept) is appended to
# state/archive/closeout-aged-out.<YYYYMMDD>.tsv first, then the file is swapped
# under locks/closeout-aged-out.lock. A row whose dir has no parseable stamp is
# kept, and so is one whose build dir still exists at any age: pipeline-health
# re-records that dir every tick, so archiving it would move the growth into
# state/archive/ rather than end it.
#CLOSEOUT_TSV_KEEP_DAYS=30
# How old a file in locks/ must be before it is even considered for deletion.
# Age alone never deletes one: no open fd in /proc and a successful flock -n are
# both required, and the unlink happens inside that lock.
#LOCK_STALE_H=24
# How long state/leases/ must be untouched before the dead directory is removed.
# state/quota/leases/ is a different path and is never a candidate.
#LEASES_STALE_D=7
# How old scratch under tmp/ must be before stage 8 sweeps it: a
# blocked-resolver fix-round worktree (tmp/brfix/*) or a state-backup staging
# dir (tmp/state-backup.*). AGE IS THE BACKSTOP, NEVER THE DECISION — the
# resolver removes its own worktree on every exit a shell can catch, so this
# stage only ever sees what a SIGKILL, an OOM or a power cut left, and the
# longest possible round is about 2.5 hours. THE CWD PROBE IS THE GUARD: a
# candidate is kept whenever a /proc/<pid>/cwd points into it or a
# run-build/run-triage/agent-call cmdline names it, at any age.
# tmp/batch-resolve/<slug> is NOT swept at any age — it is a reused blob:none
# clone cache, so deleting it buys a re-clone.
#TMP_SCRATCH_STALE_H=24

